  "body": "Reading https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/28cdb47e557c814fcca60759f4cce43e9c0e9a47 an error: the <anchor> tag for \"#time-origin\" (https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#time-origin) does not point to \"#sec-time-origin\" (https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#sec-time-origin).\r\n\r\nI do not know if to `blame` (https://git-scm.com/docs/git-blame) W3.org or WHATWG.org specifically. I am scared to do the code (just lines https://github.com/whatwg/dom/blob/28cdb47e557c814fcca60759f4cce43e9c0e9a47/dom.bs#L36, https://github.com/whatwg/dom/blob/28cdb47e557c814fcca60759f4cce43e9c0e9a47/dom.bs#L570 {basically add/remove of \"`sec`\" is the language/spelling problem?} I think?), honestly I need a second opinion publicly before I make a change like that.\r\n\r\nAutomatic bug generation text [From \"File an issue about the selected text.\" tool]:\r\n\r\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#ref-for-time-origin\r\n\r\n> time origin",
